# Reymon LibTV Workflow — Cursor Project Rules

Before planning or executing any ad reverse-engineering, scriptwriting, prompt authoring, or LibTV canvas task in this workspace, read `AGENTS.md` in full and load the relevant skills under `.agents/skills/`:

- `.agents/skills/reymon-ad-reverse-workflow/SKILL.md` (main V3.0 orchestration & 6-stage flow)
- `.agents/skills/commercial-image-prompt-pro/SKILL.md` (8-layer optical/PBR image prompt protocol)
- `.agents/skills/cinematic-storyboard-director/SKILL.md` (V3.0 Dual-Mode video storyboard & audio sync)
- Product SKU briefs & real packshot/granule assets live in `products/` (e.g. `products/reymon-cat-litter/`).

## Non-Negotiable Safety & Quality Invariants
1. **Stage 0 4-Question Intake Gate**: Always align Product/SKU, Production Mode (`Mode A: Full-AI Unified` vs `Mode B: Hook-AI + Real-Shoot Hybrid`), A/B Hook Strategy, and Core Pain Points/CTA before drafting scripts.
2. **Zero Auto-Spend (`run=false`)**: Never pass `--run` to `libtv` CLI or `run=true` to LibTV MCP creation calls unless the user explicitly asks to trigger a specific node.
3. **Default 480p Draft Preset**: Pre-wire video nodes as `Seedance 2.5 Flash` (`star-video2.5-flash`), `resolution="480p"`, `ratio="9:16"`; static images as `Lib Image 2.6 Pro` (`lib-image-2.6-s`).
4. **Audio/BGM & Speech-Rate Lock**: Enforce `4.0~4.2` Chinese chars/sec per shot duration, lock identical `Minimax-speech-2.8-hd` `voiceId` + `speed`, and strictly forbid per-shot BGM (`No BGM`) in every video node prompt.

To enable Cursor project-local skill discovery if needed, run `python3 scripts/setup.py --agent cursor --scope project` (or `--check` for health diagnostics).
